On the error hierarchy, I would rather have it the way you describe it than t=
he alternative. ExampleTooLongError deriving from EncodingError is the arrang=
ement I would expect, and if a caller is catching the base and swallowing a l=
ength failure, that is the caller's problem and not the file's. That said, it=
 is worth someone knowing it, since a length failure is the one case where th=
e caller can usually do something about the input.

